ing immediacy, mapping the growth first of her consciousness, then, in adolescence, of her sexuality, and later, as a young woman, of her political beliefs. The African landscape (described with great lyricism), her often angry and combative relationship with her parents, her intense awareness of her own body, her passionate involvement with other people and indeed with everything around her are all here very, very powerfully present.\"--BOOK JACKET. \"Under My Skin shows a woman uncompromising, from the beginning, in every aspect, who breaks all the rules, who battles at every turn against her upbringing and environment, who looks on the world clear and hard; and yet who also displays a softness, a wonderful sense of humor, a compassion for human failure.\"--BOOK JACKET.","publicationYear":1994,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Women authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"English Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Autobiographie","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Lessing, doris, 1919-2013","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-under-my-skin-volume-one-of-my-autobiography-to-1949-doris-lessing"},{"s